		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">36</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Based on the above descriptions, let us start building the algorithm. Take a paper and start writing down.
1. Take rank
2. Check if rank is less than 1200
3. If yes, then the result is ABC
4. Otherwise, check if rank is less than 2800
5. If yes, then the result is ARC
6. Otherwise the result is AGC

This is what happens in your mind. But these are very small steps, so you don't notice them.
For a computer, we have to tell each and every small step. That is what an algorithm does.</attribute>
			<section name="graphics">
				<attribute key="x" type="double">1468.6771825396825</attribute>
				<attribute key="y" type="double">2809.2701600511828</attribute>
